safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:57PM MDT until October 24 at 3:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthwestern Hinsdale County in southwestern Colorado...\nLa Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 345 PM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations continues. Several structures are\nflooded, and numerous roads remain closed due to widespread\nflooding impacts.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 350 PM MDT, emergency management reported numerous reports of\ndamage and flooding impacts. Rivers continue to run fast and high\nand will be slow to recede. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to\n1 inch are possible across the warned area from thunderstorms\ndeveloping this afternoon, overnight and redeveloping tomorrow.\nPeriods of heavy rainfall will increase the threat of flooding\nand flash flooding .\n- This includes the following rivers...\nAnimas River, La Plata, Los Pinos, and Vallecito Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, Bayfield, Ignacio, La Plata, Falfa, Oxford, Bondad,\nHesperus, Breen, Vallecito, Mayday, Kline, Marvel, Tiffany,\nAllison and Redmesa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends"